# Busy-state interrupts: queue a follow-up while kiln is working, then
# cancel mid-turn with esc, then redirect the next turn.
@real
@size 140x45
@fixture qa/fixtures/real/wf-interrupts
WAITFOR /describe a task/ 30
SHOT ready
SEND Write a paragraph (at least 150 words) in notes.md explaining, from first principles, how a hash table resolves collisions with open addressing versus chaining, with a worked example of each.
WAITFOR /esc to stop/ 30
SHOT busy
SEND Also mention Robin Hood hashing in a short final paragraph.
WAIT 2
SHOT queued-followup
EXPECT /queue a follow-up/
KEY esc
WAIT 2
SHOT after-esc
TURN Actually, stop that and just create an empty file called done.txt instead.
SHOT redirected
RUN test -f {PROJ}/done.txt
